# Build context for docker/lab/Dockerfile (docs/research/docker-jupyter-env.md §6.4).
# The context is sent to the daemon before the first instruction runs, so anything
# left in here is paid for on every build. `target/` alone is several GiB, and the
# build stage compiles from scratch into a BuildKit cache mount anyway.

/target
/.git
/.github
/.claude
/.vscode

# The website, brand assets and packaging output — nothing the Linux build reads.
# (`artwork/` is a Windows-only build input: the `.exe` icon via `winresource`.)
/site
/artwork
/dist
/infra

# Coverage report for SonarQube (~2 MB).
/lcov.info

# The prose documentation is large and the image needs none of it — except
# `docs/legal/`, which the binary compiles in: shared/credits.rs pulls the Russian
# licence and disclaimer through `include_str!`. Excluding the whole directory
# turns a 10-minute build into a compile error at the very end.
/docs
!/docs/legal

# `dictionaries/`, `locales/`, `syntaxes/` and `tests/fixtures/` are deliberately
# NOT excluded: the first is copied next to the binary (the deb layout, P1), the
# other three are compiled in via `include_str!`/`include_bytes!` or `build.rs`.

*.bak
